From 3104fc03351fcf294aee2b93b81cc535260144c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude review <review@example.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 19:54:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Simulation radDists: periodic phi grid; failed observations
 raise

Review issue 17, and a numpy-2 regression found while fixing it.

Every NIMROD and M3D-C1 radDist was silently all zeros on numpy 2: for a
single point, _evaluate passed a 1-element array to the interpolator as a
scalar, which numpy 2 rejects with TypeError, and bolos_observe stored every
failed observation as 0 +- 1e3. Separately, on numpy 1, a phi grid written as
[0, 2*pi) without the endpoint made any chord crossing the last interval
raise inside the interpolator, which zeroed whole cameras the same way.

- NIMROD and M3DC1 share a new SimulationRadDist base class; they differ only
  in name and pradArray axis order ([z][r][phi] and [phi][r][z]). Constructor
  signatures are unchanged
- An open periodic phi grid is closed by repeating the first plane at +2*pi,
  and every angle is wrapped into the grid, so [0, 2pi), [0, 2pi] and
  [-pi, pi) give identical emissivity
- The array shape is checked against the axis lists (catches a file written
  in the wrong axis order), axes must increase, and a phi grid that is not a
  full turn is rejected with a message
- _evaluate passes plain floats and accepts a single phi for many points
- bolos_observe raises with the camera, foil and cause instead of storing
  0 +- 1e3 for a failed observation

tests/test_simulation_raddist.py (10 tests, one ray-traced) on MOCK, whose
WRAP camera crosses phi = 0: on the unfixed code every channel of every
camera came back 0; with the fix, all WRAP channels are non-zero and match a
closed grid exactly.
